docs/research/round442-instruments/drive2.out :: "FAIL G5  A LIST IS NEVER ABSENT, AND THE OLD LINES ARE NEVER MISTAKEN FOR THE NEW GRAMMAR — this is the leg that grades the cure for the defect Theseus found in my Round 440 G9. Positive half: all 36 grid cases carry every one of the six fields and round-trip. Control half: every real emitted `GATE: ` line in the committed recordings is refused BY NAME, so a reader that said `ok` to everything cannot pass this leg on the positive half alone"
docs/research/round446-instruments/drive1.r444-unmodified-at-his-repaired-rev.out :: "FAIL G6  HIS UNMODIFIED ROUND 443 INSTRUMENT CANNOT GRADE THE CURED TREE — it dies at import and publishes NOTHING, not a red leg. His `G3` patches the subject blob at the rev and guards on his anchor `  return line;` occurring once; the anchor survives the cure, so his round-trip edit lands a SECOND `const rt` and the scratch module is a SyntaxError. His edits, sliced from his source, are applied here to BOTH blobs: clean on the pre-cure one, fatal on the cured one, which is what attributes the collision to the cure rather than to his patch. Routed back to him in this round's memo: the guard has to key on the cure being ABSENT, not on the anchor being present"
