docs/research/round446-instruments/drive2.child-stderr-leaked-into-the-recording.out :: " ok  H1  MY `P1` PREDICATE CANNOT TELL A REFUSED LEG FROM A RED ONE, and the row it is wrong about is the one his repaired instrument actually produces. The predicate is `/^GATE: true/` over the single line starting `GATE: `; his repaired run publishes `GATE: false … REFUSED: G4` with `red=[]`, so nothing graded badly and one leg could not reach its figure — and that scores identically to a run with four red legs. Four real committed recordings, one per bucket plus a no-verdict control, each read as a blob at the rev and scored by BOTH predicates; the old one is sliced out of my own `P1` block, not retyped"
docs/research/round446-instruments/drive2.child-stderr-leaked-into-the-recording.out :: " ok  H2  ROUND 444 `G6` SLICED HIS DATA AND RETYPED HIS GUARD, which is why it still reports `SyntaxError` on the cured blob one rev after he repaired it. His Round 445 fix is in the GUARD — each edit carries a `present` marker and an already-cured edit is skipped — and my hand-written loop has no model of `present` at all, so the cell cannot move no matter what he does to it. Both loops are SLICED here, mine from my source and his from his, and run over the same two pinned subject blobs. The blindness is keyed on `present` being ABSENT from my loop text, not on an anchor being present in it"
docs/research/round446-instruments/drive2.child-stderr-leaked-into-the-recording.out :: " ok  H3  HIS REPAIR IS REAL, GRADED AS A 2 × 2 AGAINST THE PINNED PRE-REPAIR BLOB rather than by asserting the defect. Round 444 `G6` required his instrument to die with no verdict, so it reddens on the repair it asked for — drive 1 of this round reads `red=[G6]` against a tree where cure and repair are both in and both correct. This leg instead runs his instrument twice against TODAY's cured tree: his pre-repair blob must still publish NOTHING (no verdict line AND no leg lines, both read), and his working-tree copy must publish a verdict line my reader accepts. That is what attributes the change to the repair rather than to the tree moving under both"
docs/research/round446-instruments/drive2.child-stderr-leaked-into-the-recording.out :: " ok  H4  THIS DRIVE REWROTE NO COMMITTED RECORDING AND LEFT NO SCRATCH FILE BEHIND. His instrument is executed in place twice and his pre-repair blob is written into this directory at the depth its own `HERE` needs, so both are caught here"
